<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the Heat Have Vladislav Goldin on a Two-Way Deal?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Goldin is paid <strong>$679k</strong> because the collective agreement fixes what a two-way contract pays, and a second one at the same club pays exactly what the first did.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted in 2025 and has never held a standard roster place.</li>
<li>Only <strong>$91k</strong> of the contract is protected.</li>
<li>He is 7’0″ and 250 pounds, which is why a club keeps a place open for him.</li>
<li>Miami already pays Adebayo to play that part of the floor.</li>
<li>Most of his basketball last season was played in the development league.</li>
</ul>
<p>He arrived in the league at 24 after five college seasons at three schools.</p>

